=== Origins of High Science ===
High Science, often referred to as ''« The Corporation »'' by its employees, was a small nuclear research institute established in early 1965 by Gabriel Blackwood and a couple of his fellow colleagues. Driven by the narrative of a fusion-powered future that Blackwood ingrained into his team's minds, the team worked tirelessly to prove the feasibility of fusion energy. Backed by a board of investors from the Federation of Vardun, High Science had all the resources it required.
[[Founded|1981|Chaos Forces]]
February 2nd 1973, High Science successfully produced the first energy from a fusion power source, proving that fusion power is a reality rather than science-fiction. The media flocked to this discovery, deeming Blackwood as the "father of fusion", idolising him.
[[CPUF|founded|1973]]
Shortly after this discovery, the Proxy Wars between the Republic and Vardun broke out, and it destroyed the economy. Deprived of its primary source of financial support from Vardun, High Science struggled to afford the soaring prices of an inflated market. By May 1973, High Science had declared bankruptcy, and was abandoned.
=== The Formation of the Chaos Forces ===
In early March 1981, the ''« ████ █████ »'' was quietly announced to the heads of departments. Many saw that this moved The Corporation in the wrong direction; however it was not their place to interject. Word quickly spread about this new development, and it lead many people who believed in High Science's vision to leave as they no longer felt they could support what they were working for anymore. They were already on edge with how classified and "hush-hush" all scientific findings were to be kept, believing that such information should be shared for the betterment of everyone. 
=== High Science Private Security ===
HSPS, or ''« High Science Private Security »'', is among the most professional and drilled para-military group on the Malverrian continent.
[[Founded|fall|1975]]
Established in the fall of 1975, this sub-division was put under the management of the ''« Department of Defence »'', a corporate Department within High Science. 
=== The Experimental Design Bureau 14 ===
This facility, commonly nicknamed the ''« Classified Part-Underground Facility »'' by its employees, is located somewhere deep in the mountains of the Democratic Republic of Malverra. Construction was completed around March 1979, marking its official opening to all employees. Although the facility's origins remain relatively unknown, its creation can be traced back as far as the winter of 1975.
== Past Lore ==
The original lore written by Daeny, largely outdated and inaccurate today. It is kept here for archival's sake, and for reference while the new lore covers all main points. 

=== Creation of High Science ===
High Science is a nuclear company established in early 1979 that develops and promotes in the field of nuclear activities.

The future creator of High Science under the title Mr. D decided to make a group of advanced scientists. He was an experienced nuclear physicist, but it was very difficult for him to create High Science alone, and then he invited his familiar nuclear physicists to join the creation. Only a small number joined the creation (about 5-7 people).

In 1980 they designed the creation and testing of very small thermonuclear installations in a small facility. During an experiment they recorded their achievement and share to other nuclear physics. This caused a wave of popularity and several more people joined High Science. Some people started to invest massively to continue the development of High Science.

After half of year, when there were enough funds Mr. D with other advanced scientists decided to create a much larger facility to create, test and design there.
{{public}}
=== Creation of CPUF ===
In the spring of 1982, an underground facility called the Classified Part Underground Facility was built by High Science in order to study, test, and create or invent new thermonuclear technologies.

The most famous achievement, titled “Project ‘Little Sun’”, was the most well-known creation and is the main focus of the facility. However, any other data, including even its name, is classified. Inside the facility also contains a standard fission reactor (however not operable yet in the game, currently), experimental workspaces for crystal testing and evaluation, as well as a Crystal Testing Lab where different crystals are looked into with more detail, as well as a Rocket Testing Facility. Although not much is known about it, it may have something to do with High Science’s next creation, revealed to be an interstellar spaceship.

=== Creation of Private Security ===
Private security is a group of hired professional guards who defend the facility from any threats.

In 1982 the Classified Part Underground Facility did not have professional defense from threats, but the end of 1982 has changed it a lot.

At the end of 1982 a large raid was carried out on the Classified Part Underground Facility. The simple security tried to defeat the Chaos Forces, but they failed, and the Chaos Forces entered a few sections of the facility. It was good that there was a lock down system and that Chaos Forces failed to enter the main sections of the facility, but they entered Sector C-2. Many of them were locked down in this area.

After few hours, Mr. D was reported about the raid and he decided to destroy Sector C-2. After the destruction of Sector C-2, Mr. D hired a private professional security team and said that they should arrive as soon as they can.

A private security team arrived after 5 hours. They cleared the facility of all the Chaos Forces that were in it. After this incident, the facility became better defended: was added more defense systems, the employee verification process was tightened and more hidden surveillance cameras.

=== Creation of Chaos Forces ===
In the summer of 1982, at the Classified Part Underground Facility a small part of the participants voluntarily left the company, taking some of the important facility's data. After a few months, they began to raid the facility. They called themselves 'Chaos Forces' and their goal was to get 'High Science' achievements and destroy the Classified Part Underground Facility.

After Chaos Forces attacks High Science decided to improve the security system. High Science tried to eliminate Chaos Forces, but their location was unknown.

=== Computer Core ===
In the middle of 1982, a computer core was built in the Sector B, engineering zone. It is responsible for most of the systems and functions in the facility such as: defense system, management of the thermonuclear reactor, server management, notification system management, etc. Basically, the computer core was built for the automatic control of a starship that is in development. In 1983, testing is planned in which observations of the operation of the computer core and its actions in unforeseen situations will be carried out. If the testing will be successful, it will be a step towards the success of creating an automatic starship. At the moment, some computer core functions and systems are disabled to prepare for testing.

Only administration, security personnel and engineers with special access can enter the computer core zone.

=== T-SD-02 Protocol ===
In early 1983, the T-SD-02 protocol was developed. It represents the complete destruction within a radius of 3-5 kilometers by detonating a computer core. This protocol was created for the self-destruction of a starship that is in development in the event of an imminent fall.

The first version of the protocol was failed during a testing.

=== Abandoned Warhead ===
A warhead was developed in 1981. It is a prototype of the 3rd warhead created by High Science. The purpose of the warhead is the complete destruction of the underground section of the facility. Its activation occurs only in dangerous situations that are inevitable in the underground part of the facility.

The warhead was built in the Classified Part Underground Facility in 1982, but in a few months it was abandoned for unknown reasons. It is only known that there was a collapse and destruction of the staircase that led to the warhead chamber. The warhead was fully disengaged and disarmed to avoid starting a nuclear reaction that would lead to the complete destruction of the underground section of the facility.

It is located in sector C in the maintenance corridors. Only security personnel are allowed to enter the warhead area. Entry for other persons working in the facility only for engineering / technical personnel with a special access level.

At the moment, it is planned to dismantle the warhead and control it by the end of 1983.

=== The Democratic Republic of Mountainland ===
The year is 1983. The Democratic Republic of Mountainland is going through difficult times. Unemployment is high, and citizens' lives are full of difficulties. The Cold War with the Vulcanic Federation, which began in 1981, casts a long shadow over the country.

The United Nations of the Northern States remains neutral in this conflict, but is reluctant to assist the Vulcanic Federation. The Mountainland is too far behind in many fields, but at the same time leading position in thermonuclear science thanks to High Science. High Science, which became famous in 1982 after the creation of the Classified Part Underground Facility, aims to create an experimental thermonuclear reactor. The goal is to keep the reactor stable for a shift and successfully make gigawatts of energy. The government of the country realized the potential of High Science and began to invest in its development.

The success of the experimental reactor means a revolution in energy. If the experiment would be successful, the reactor will be constantly operating, providing energy to hundreds of cities and factories in the republic. This could be a turning point in history.

[[Category:Experiemental Controlled Fusion Reactor]]

Originally, the area where the facility now stands was intended to become a mine, supplying High Science's other endeavours with lithium ore. However by the summer of 1976, radioactive crystals were found in the caverns where mining operations were taking place. Temporary laboratories were set up in these caverns to investigate their potential, and all mining was halted. By the end of 1977, the crystals had been found to possess remarkable amounts of radiation - deadly amounts, even. 

Following this discovery, High Science decided to construct a permanent facility at the site. It was proposed that a new experimental version of a reactor prototype developed by High Science prior to the acquisition, known as the ''« Little Sun »'' would be built here. The project was then designated the ''« Experimental Controlled-Fusion Reactor »'', or ECFR.

In the late spring of 1982, a daring raid by the Chaos Forces began on the facility. For 12 long months after their initial defection from High Science, the Chaos Forces planned and prepared for their assault on the facility - with many knowledgeable about the facility’s maze-like layout. Both High Science and HSPS leadership were aware of the threat that the newly formed Chaos Forces posed; yet, the possibility of a full scale, and organised assault on the facility was an idea that if ever considered, was considered a punchline. As such, HSPS forces were only organised within High Science Corporate Headquarters, due to their perceived vulnerability. A more *primitive* team of security called the ''« Patrol Team »'' are established at every High Science facility, however later they proved not to be enough to stop the Chaos Forces.

Even before the first concrete began to be poured on site - large deposits of munitions were buried - with explosive triggers ready to be detonated by wire, a revolutionary design called ''« ██████ ████████ »''. It was on a foundation of explosives that the CPUF was built.

During the Chaos Forces raid on April 3rd 1982, following a call made by the Facility Director of EDB14 to ███  █████, he sent the order to detonate Sector C-2, and 25 minutes later, █████s arrived on site. Many of the Chaos Forces along with several employees were caught in the blast and ensuing collapse.

This incident, among others, ultimately led to the permanent installation of the HSPS & more detection systems: from security cameras to motion detectors. Soon after the incident, the computer core program effectively doubled in both staff and funding assigned. Additionally, in the summer of 1982, a series of security installations both outside and inside the facility began construction, to aid the HSPS in the fight to protect High Science's interests.

Established April 18th 1981, the  ''« Chaos Forces »'' were a group of ex-employees who no longer trusted High Science's motives, and wanted to expose High Science's secrets to the world. The Corporation wasn't *truly* working for ''« The Power Of The Republic »'' as they so desperately advertised, and the Chaos Forces knew that. They had to reveal the truth.

The Chaos Forces weren't entirely compromised of ex-employees, and not all Chaos Forces members joined the ''« Chaos Forces Alliance »''. The Chaos Forces Alliance is only for the best Chaos Forces operatives who know the most about the facility and its operations. Typically, these members were ex-employees from higher echelons of The Corporation, the architects, heads of departments and those who know more information than High Science would like them to; hence their strive for publicising the truth about High Science, and their ████ █████.

It was April 3rd 1982, a day like any other. The Chaos Forces had devised a plan, a plan that had been nicknamed « The Directive », sometimes referred to as Directive 7A-83. Whilst its true meaning is still unknown by High Science's intelligence, it was a coordinated attack on The Corporation's 14th Experimental Design Bureau - the same Bureau at which the majority of apprehended Chaos Forces members were once employed.

An account from a member of the Patrol Team on site that day claimed that around half an hour after the raid started, teams of "Militarised Personnel" arrived on site. These people did not take kindly to those who bore a gun.

Originally started by passionate physicists who believed in Blackwood's vision, High Science was quietly acquired by an unknown shell corporation in 1975, and since then, little is known about it publicly.
